# The CHUNKWISE GATED-DELTA-NET triad's circular buffer table.
#
#   kernels/resident_gdnc_{reader,compute,writer}.c, program `gdnc`.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EVERY BUFFER IS Float32, AND THAT IS A WHOLE-PROGRAM DECISION RATHER THAN SIX
# INDEPENDENT ONES
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `tools/emit_tensix_cb_formats.py`'s `conditional_destination_format()` scans EVERY CB:
# a Float32 buffer unpacks into Tf32 source registers only when `dst_accum_mode` is on AND
# every CB in the table is named Float32. ONE bf16 buffer anywhere demotes every Float32 CB's
# `unpack_dst` to Float16_b -- which would put the rolled window, the conv weight and the
# banded matmul's accumulator on bf16 mantissas with nothing anywhere saying so. Measured on
# the decode family 2026-08-21; it is why the fp32<->bf16 bridge is TWO SEPARATE PROGRAMS
# (`render_widen` / `render_narrow`) and not a mixed table.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `dst_accum_mode 1` IS MANDATORY, NOT PREFERRED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This op carries the rolling conv window ACROSS CHUNKS. A 16-bit destination accumulator
# re-rounds the banded matmul's `2*taps`-term sum once per chunk, and the error is the next
# chunk's initial condition -- the same argument `gdn_float32.cbtable` makes about the
# recurrent state, on a shorter carry.
#
# IT ALSO SETS THE DST CEILING AT FOUR. DST is 16 tiles of 32x32; DST_SYNC half hands MATH one
# half at a time and accum mode halves it again. `product_batch()` in the compute kernel
# clamps to that and to a divisor of `2*taps`; a batch above the ceiling would silently alias
# DST tiles onto each other and produce a smoothly wrong convolution.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `math_fidelity 4` IS NOT FREE HERE AND IS STILL RIGHT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fidelity phases become MOP inner loops, so the banded matmul costs four passes rather than
# one. It is kept because the products it multiplies are the model's activations against its
# conv weights, at the head of a 24-layer recurrence -- the same place the decode family
# spends it. `MATMUL_INNER_LOOPS` in the compute kernel is derived from this number, so
# lowering it here changes the emitted MOP and nothing else has to change.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE CB MAP -- see resident_gdnc_protocol.h for what each one carries
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   cb  0  CB_IN      the chunk's input tile column. Reader-produced.
#   cb  1  CB_STATE   the ASSEMBLED window tile: row p is window plane p's row 0. Reader-
#                     produced, and ZEROED ONCE at residency boot so rows taps-1..31 -- which
#                     every band matrix multiplies by a zero column -- can never hold a NaN.
#   cb  2  CB_BAND    the `2*taps` constant 0/1 band tiles. Pushed ONCE per descriptor and
#                     popped at the end of it, so the buffer is empty at every descriptor
#                     boundary and its push is an exact hit on the limit.
#   cb  3  CB_VECTOR  this column's `taps` ROW-REPLICATED conv weight tiles.
#   cb  4  CB_PROD    the `2*taps` weighted products. THERE IS NO FMA -- `mul_tiles_init`
#                     passes `acc_to_dest=true` and the LLK hardcodes it to a literal zero for
#                     ELWMUL on every path -- so every product is packed here and read back by
#                     the matmul. The COMPUTE thread is its only producer.
#   cb  5  CB_WORK    PHASE DELTA only: the compute thread's nine `[C,S]` working groups.
#                     ITS OWN INDEX AND NOT CB_IN'S, and that is the decode family's most
#                     expensive lesson respelled: a buffer has ONE PRODUCER for the life of a
#                     residency, because a dataflow `cb_push_back` INCREMENTS the stream
#                     register while the compute one keeps a LOCAL counter and STORES over it.
#                     Sharing a buffer between the two makes `received - acked` wrap to a huge
#                     unsigned and `cb_wait_front` stop blocking, SILENTLY, for a whole run.
#   cb  6  CB_SCRATCH PHASE DELTA only: the READER's private page for the gate block. NEVER
#                     PUSHED and never popped -- the staging idiom writes through a write
#                     pointer without reserving, which is safe only while that pointer is
#                     provably at the buffer base.
#   cb  7  CB_DECAY   PHASE DELTA only: this head's `[C,C]` decay-ratio tile, built on the
#                     HOST because a card-built one costs the whole precision advantage of
#                     going chunkwise (8.6e-03 -> 1.7e-02, modelled through this unpack).
#   cb  8  CB_CC      PHASE DELTA only: the `[C,C]` working tiles -- two Gram matrices, the
#                     causal mask and the twelve Newton tiles. Compute-produced.
#   cb 16  CB_OUT     CONV: two pages a column, the conv_out tile then the RAW input tile the
#                     writer takes the window roll's `taps-1` rows out of.
#                     DELTA: per head, `state_tiles` y tiles then `state_tiles^2` state tiles.
#                     Either way the ORDER IS THE WIRE CONTRACT the writer's split is defined
#                     over.
#
#   Format: tools/emit_tensix_cb_formats.py
#   cb <index> <format> <tile_r> <tile_c> <face_r> <num_faces>

math_fidelity  4
approx         0
dst_accum_mode 1

cb  0  Float32 32 32 16 4
cb  1  Float32 32 32 16 4
cb  2  Float32 32 32 16 4
cb  3  Float32 32 32 16 4
cb  4  Float32 32 32 16 4
cb  5  Float32 32 32 16 4
cb  6  Float32 32 32 16 4
cb  7  Float32 32 32 16 4
cb  8  Float32 32 32 16 4
cb 16  Float32 32 32 16 4
